---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../site';
---

<!-- Draft revised November 2026 to match how the site works. Have it reviewed by a legal advisor before relying on it. -->
<Page
  title="Privacy Policy | Palm Readings AI"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Palm Readings AI collects, uses, and protects your information, including the hand photos you upload."
  eyebrow="Last Updated and Effective as of November 10, 2026"
>
  <div class="prose-page">
    <h2>Who We Are</h2>
    <p>
      Palm Readings AI ("Palm Readings," "we," "us," or "our") operates the Palm Readings AI website (palmreadings.ai) and
      related digital services (the "site" or "services"). Our goal is to provide a private, reflective, and accessible
      experience for individuals seeking insight, self-awareness, and perspective through digital palm readings.
    </p>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and the choices you
      have. By using the site, you agree to the practices described here.
    </p>

    <h2>The Short Version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your hand photos are sent to our AI service provider to create your reading. <strong>We do not store your photos.</strong> They are discarded once your reading is created.</li>
      <li>We do not use your photos to identify you, and we do not create biometric templates or identifiers from them.</li>
      <li>Your finished reading is kept only in your own browser for that session. We do not keep a copy on our servers.</li>
      <li>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p><strong>When you request a reading</strong>, we collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Photos of your hands (and, for couples readings, of your partner’s hands)</li>
      <li>Which hand you write with, and the type of reading you choose</li>
      <li>Optional details you choose to give: first name, age, and pronouns</li>
      <li>Whether you choose to include marriage and children predictions</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>When you contact us</strong>, we collect your name, email address, and anything you include in your message.</p>
    <p><strong>When you give feedback</strong> on a reading, we collect your rating, any comment you write, and the type of reading it was about.</p>
    <p>
      <strong>Automatically</strong>, as with most websites, we and our service providers receive technical information such
      as your IP address, browser type, device type, operating system, referring pages, access times, and how you interact
      with the site.
    </p>

    <h2>How Your Hand Photos Are Handled</h2>
    <p>
      Your photos are resized on your own device, then sent securely to our servers and on to our AI service provider,
      which analyzes the visible features of your hands (such as hand shape, lines, and mounts) to create your reading.
      Your optional name, age, and pronouns are included so the reading can address you personally.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>We process your photos only to create the reading you asked for.</li>
      <li>We do not save your photos to any database or storage, and they are discarded once your reading is created.</li>
      <li>We do not use your photos to recognize or identify you, and we do not extract or keep hand geometry, palm prints, or any other biometric identifier.</li>
      <li>We use our AI providers’ business API services and do not opt in to any program that lets them use your photos to train their models.</li>
      <li>Our AI provider may briefly retain requests under its own policies (for example, to detect abuse) before deleting them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Because hand images can be considered sensitive or biometric information in some places, we ask for your consent
      before any photo is uploaded. If you upload photos of another person, such as a partner, you must have their
      permission to do so.
    </p>

    <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To create and deliver the readings you request</li>
      <li>To respond to your messages and support requests</li>
      <li>To understand how the site is used and improve our readings, content, and features</li>
      <li>To keep the site secure and prevent abuse</li>
      <li>To comply with legal obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sharing Information with Service Providers</h2>
    <p>We share information only with service providers that help us run the site, and only as needed for them to do so:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>AI service providers</strong>, which analyze your photos and write your reading</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which hosts the site and protects it from attacks</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong>, for analytics (Google Analytics) and for our email and records of feedback and contact messages (Google Workspace)</li>
      <li><strong>Email delivery services</strong>, which deliver contact form messages to us</li>
      <li><strong>Payment processors</strong>, if you purchase a paid reading. Payments are handled directly by the processor; we do not see or store your full card number.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may also disclose information if required by law, or if we believe in good faith that it is necessary to comply
      with legal obligations, protect our rights or property, or ensure user safety.
    </p>

    <h2>Usage Data and Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      We record anonymous usage information, such as which reading type was chosen and how many photos were included, to
      understand how the service is used. These records do not include your name, age, pronouns, or photos. Feedback you
      choose to submit is used to improve our readings.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics and Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the site. Google Analytics uses cookies and similar
      technologies and may collect information such as your IP address, browser and device type, referring pages, and
      on-site behavior, which we see only in aggregate. You can learn more in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>,
      and you can opt out with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The reading app also uses your browser’s session storage to keep your latest reading available if you refresh the
      page. It is stored only on your device and is cleared when you close the tab or start a new reading. You can block or
      delete cookies and site data in your browser settings.
    </p>

    <h2>How Long We Keep Information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Hand photos:</strong> not stored by us; discarded once your reading is created</li>
      <li><strong>Readings:</strong> not stored by us; kept in your browser for the session only</li>
      <li><strong>Contact messages and feedback:</strong> kept as long as needed to respond and improve the service, then deleted</li>
      <li><strong>Security and server logs:</strong> kept for a limited period by our hosting provider</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Security of Your Information</h2>
    <p>
      We use encrypted connections (HTTPS) and take reasonable measures to protect your information from unauthorized
      access, use, or disclosure. However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is completely
      secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Choices and Rights</h2>
    <p>You can always use the site without giving your name, age, or pronouns. You may contact us at any time to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Ask what information we hold about you</li>
      <li>Request corrections or deletion of your information</li>
      <li>Opt out of non-essential emails</li>
      <li>Ask questions or raise concerns about our data practices</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights under local law, such as the right to access, correct,
      delete, or obtain a copy of your personal information. We will respond to requests as required by applicable law and
      will not discriminate against you for making one.
    </p>

    <h2>Age Requirement</h2>
    <p>
      Palm Readings AI is intended for adults. You must be 18 or older (or the age of majority where you live) to use the
      reading service. We do not knowingly collect information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with
      information, please contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to Other Websites</h2>
    <p>
      Our site may contain links to external websites. We are not responsible for the content or privacy practices of those
      sites and encourage you to review their privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Email Communications</h2>
    <p>
      If you contact us, we will reply by email. If we offer email updates, we will only send them if you sign up, and you
      can unsubscribe at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with a new "Last Updated"
      date. Continued use of the site after an update means you accept the revised policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact Information</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact us through our
      <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> or by email at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
